data.content:
## What Breaks in .NET 11

In EF Core 11 (shipping with .NET 11), the **sync-over-async opt-in for the Cosmos DB provider has been removed entirely**. The configuration option you used in .NET 10:

```csharp
options.UseCosmos(...).ConfigureWarnings(w =>
    w.Ignore(CosmosEventId.SyncNotSupported));
```

no longer suppresses the error. All synchronous LINQ operators (`ToList()`, `First()`, `Count()`, etc.) and `SaveChanges()` now throw an **`InvalidOperationException`** unconditionally against the Cosmos provider.

## Required Fix — Convert to Async

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

**Key points:**
- There is **no workaround** — the opt-in was removed, not just defaulted off.
- All callers up the stack must also become `async`/`await`.
- `Add()` remains synchronous (it's an in-memory tracking call), but `SaveChanges()` must become `SaveChangesAsync()`.
